---@meta
-- The Axcenity Engine script API, for Lua Language Server (autocomplete
-- and type hints in VS Code and other editors).
-- Generated by `cargo run -p axcenity-script --bin lua-definitions`. Don't edit by hand.

-- Values --------------------------------------------------------------------

---A position, size or direction in studs. Y is up.
---@class Vector3
---@field X number The X component.
---@field Y number The Y component (up).
---@field Z number The Z component.
---@field Magnitude number The length of the vector.
---@field Unit Vector3 The same direction with length 1 (the zero vector stays zero).
---@operator add(Vector3): Vector3
---@operator sub(Vector3): Vector3
---@operator mul(Vector3): Vector3
---@operator mul(number): Vector3
---@operator div(Vector3): Vector3
---@operator div(number): Vector3
---@operator unm: Vector3

---A color, with each channel from 0 to 1.
---@class Color3
---@field R number Red, from 0 to 1.
---@field G number Green, from 0 to 1.
---@field B number Blue, from 0 to 1.

---One UI axis as a scale and pixel offset.
---@class UDim
---@field Scale number The fraction of the parent size.
---@field Offset number The pixel offset.

---A UI position or size with scale and pixel-offset components.
---@class UDim2
---@field X UDim The horizontal component.
---@field Y UDim The vertical component.

---One choice of an enum, such as `Enum.Material.Neon`.
---@class EnumItem
---@field Name string The item's name, such as `"Neon"`.

---The player's keyboard, from `game:GetService("UserInputService")`. LocalScripts only.
---@class UserInputService
---@field InputBegan Signal Fires when a key goes down. The handler gets an InputObject and `gameProcessedEvent` (always false for now): `function(input, gameProcessedEvent) ... end`.
---@field InputEnded Signal Fires when a key comes back up, with the same arguments as InputBegan.
local UserInputServiceClass = {}

---True while `key` is held down, such as `Enum.KeyCode.W`.
---@param key EnumItem.KeyCode
---@return boolean
function UserInputServiceClass:IsKeyDown(key) end


---The game's frame loop, from `game:GetService("RunService")`.
---@class RunService
---@field Heartbeat Signal Fires once every frame, after physics. The handler gets the frame's length in seconds: `function(deltaTime) ... end`.

---One key going down or up, as `InputBegan` and `InputEnded` handlers get it.
---@class InputObject
---@field KeyCode EnumItem.KeyCode Which key, such as `Enum.KeyCode.W`.

---What the player sees through, `workspace.CurrentCamera`. LocalScripts only. Setting Position or Orientation moves the view; the player can still fly on from there.
---@class Camera
---@field Position Vector3 Where the camera is, in studs.
---@field Orientation Vector3 Which way it looks, in degrees like a Part's: X looks up (positive) and down, Y turns left (positive) and right. Z is ignored.
---@field LookVector Vector3 The direction the camera looks in, one stud long. Read-only.

