-- Instances -----------------------------------------------------------------

---Anything in the game tree. Every class below is a kind of Instance.
---@class Instance
---@field Name string The Instance's name. Children can be found by name: `workspace.Block`.
---@field ClassName string The Instance's class, such as `"Part"`. Read-only.
---@field Parent Instance? The Instance this one is inside, or nil. Setting it moves the Instance.
---@field Changed Signal Fires when a property (or `Name` or `Parent`) gets a different value, whether a script, physics or the editor changed it. The handler gets the property's name: `function(property) ... end`.
---@field ChildAdded Signal Fires when an Instance is put inside this one. The handler gets the child.
---@field ChildRemoved Signal Fires when an Instance is taken out of this one. The handler gets the child.
---@field [string] Workspace|Players|Lighting|ReplicatedStorage|ServerScriptService|StarterPlayer|StarterPlayerScripts|Part|MeshPart|Script|LocalScript|ModuleScript|RemoteEvent|Player|Model|Folder|SurfaceAppearance|ScreenGui|Frame|TextLabel|TextButton|ImageLabel|Sound|PointLight|SpotLight A child, found by its name.
local InstanceClass = {}

---The first child with this name, or nil. With `recursive`, searches every descendant.
---@param name string
---@param recursive? boolean
---@return Instance?
function InstanceClass:FindFirstChild(name, recursive) end

---An event that fires when this one property (or `Name` or `Parent`) gets a different value. The handler gets nothing: read the property to see its new value.
---@param property string
---@return Signal
function InstanceClass:GetPropertyChangedSignal(property) end

---An event, such as `part.Touched`. Connect a function to run it every time the event fires.
---@class Signal
local SignalClass = {}

---Runs `callback` every time the event fires, each time as its own task (so it may `task.wait`). Returns a Connection for stopping it.
---@param callback function
---@return Connection
function SignalClass:Connect(callback) end

---A function connected to an event, returned by `Connect`.
---@class Connection
---@field Connected boolean True until `Disconnect` is called (or the Instance is destroyed).
local ConnectionClass = {}

---Stops the function from running when the event fires again. Calling it twice is harmless.
---@return nil
function ConnectionClass:Disconnect() end

---The root of the game, called `game` in scripts.
---@class DataModel: Instance
---@field Workspace Workspace The service that holds the 3D world. Parts inside it are drawn.
---@field Players Players The service with a Player for everyone in the game.
---@field Lighting Lighting The service for the world's lighting. It sets sun shadows, the sky colors that metal parts reflect, and post-processing (exposure, tone mapping and bloom).
---@field ReplicatedStorage ReplicatedStorage The service for things Scripts and LocalScripts share, such as RemoteEvents and ModuleScripts.
---@field ServerScriptService ServerScriptService The service that holds server scripts (`scripts/*.server.lua`).
---@field StarterPlayer StarterPlayer The service with what each player starts with, such as StarterPlayerScripts.
---@field UserInputService UserInputService The player's keyboard (same as `game:GetService("UserInputService")`). LocalScripts only.
---@field RunService RunService The game's frame loop, with `Heartbeat` (same as `game:GetService("RunService")`).
local DataModelClass = {}

---The service with this class name, such as `"Players"`, `"RunService"` or `"UserInputService"`.
---@param className string
---@return Instance
function DataModelClass:GetService(className) end


---The service that holds the 3D world. Parts inside it are drawn.
---@class Workspace: Instance
---@field CurrentCamera Camera The camera the player sees through. LocalScripts only.

---The service with a Player for everyone in the game.
---@class Players: Instance
---@field LocalPlayer Player The player on this device. LocalScripts only.

---The service for the world's lighting. It sets sun shadows, the sky colors that metal parts reflect, and post-processing (exposure, tone mapping and bloom).
---@class Lighting: Instance
---@field ShadowsEnabled boolean If false, the sun casts no shadows. Turn this off on low-end machines.
---@field ShadowDistance number How far from the camera sun shadows reach, in studs. Shorter distances give sharper shadows.
---@field ShadowSoftness number How soft shadow edges are, from 0 (crisp) to 1 (very soft). Edges stay sharp where a part touches what it shades and soften further away, like real shadows.
---@field SkyTopColor Color3 The sky's color straight up.
---@field SkyHorizonColor Color3 The sky's color at the horizon.
---@field GroundColor Color3 The color of the ground below the horizon, as the sky and reflections see it.
---@field EnvironmentIntensity number How strongly the sky lights and is reflected by parts. 0 turns it off.
---@field PostProcessingEnabled boolean If false, the scene is drawn with no tone mapping or bloom.
---@field Exposure number Brightens or darkens the whole image before tone mapping. 1 is neutral.
---@field BloomEnabled boolean If false, bright parts don't glow.
---@field BloomIntensity number How strong the glow around bright parts is.
---@field BloomThreshold number How bright a pixel must be before it glows.

---The service for things Scripts and LocalScripts share, such as RemoteEvents and ModuleScripts.
---@class ReplicatedStorage: Instance

---The service that holds server scripts (`scripts/*.server.lua`).
---@class ServerScriptService: Instance

---The service with what each player starts with, such as StarterPlayerScripts.
---@class StarterPlayer: Instance

---Holds the LocalScripts (`scripts/*.client.lua`), which run on the player's side.
---@class StarterPlayerScripts: Instance

---A solid shape in the world.
---@class Part: Instance
---@field Anchored boolean If true, the part stays where it is. If false, it falls and collides with other parts.
---@field Shape EnumItem.PartType|"Block"|"Ball"|"Cylinder"|"Wedge" Block, Ball, Cylinder (along X) or Wedge.
---@field Position Vector3 Where the part's center is, in studs. Setting it on an unanchored part teleports it and stops it moving.
---@field Orientation Vector3 Rotation in degrees around X, Y and Z, applied Z first, then X, then Y.
---@field Size Vector3 The part's size in studs along X, Y and Z.
---@field Color Color3 The part's color.
---@field Material EnumItem.Material|"Plastic"|"Metal"|"Glass"|"Neon" Plastic, Metal, Glass (see-through) or Neon (glows). Setting it resets Metalness and Roughness.
---@field Metalness number From 0 (not metal) to 1 (metal).
---@field Roughness number From 0 (mirror-smooth) to 1 (matte).
---@field CastShadow boolean If false, the part casts no sun shadow. It's still shaded by other parts' shadows.
---@field Touched Signal Fires when another part starts touching this one, once per new contact (not every frame while they touch). The handler gets the other part: `part.Touched:Connect(function(otherPart) ... end)`.

---A solid 3D model imported from a glTF or FBX file, drawn with the file's own materials (or its SurfaceAppearances'). It collides as the model's convex hull.
---@class MeshPart: Instance
---@field Anchored boolean If true, the part stays where it is. If false, it falls and collides with other parts.
---@field MeshId string The model's glTF or FBX file, inside the project folder, such as "assets/models/chair.glb"; `#` after it picks objects in the file ("assets/models/props.fbx#Bench"). The editor's Import Model sets it.
---@field Position Vector3 Where the center of the model's box is, in studs. Setting it on an unanchored part teleports it and stops it moving.
---@field Orientation Vector3 Rotation in degrees around X, Y and Z, applied Z first, then X, then Y.
---@field Size Vector3 The size of the model's box in studs along X, Y and Z. The model stretches to fill it.
---@field CastShadow boolean If false, the part casts no sun shadow. It's still shaded by other parts' shadows.
---@field Touched Signal Fires when another part starts touching this one, once per new contact (not every frame while they touch). The handler gets the other part: `part.Touched:Connect(function(otherPart) ... end)`.

---Lua code that runs on the server, from a `.server.lua` file.
---@class Script: Instance

---Lua code that runs on the player's side (input, camera), from a `.client.lua` file.
---@class LocalScript: Instance

---Lua code that scripts load with `require`, from a `.module.lua` file. It runs once per side and returns one value.
---@class ModuleScript: Instance

---Carries messages between Scripts and LocalScripts. Keep it in ReplicatedStorage.
---@class RemoteEvent: Instance
---@field OnServerEvent Signal Fires when a LocalScript calls `FireServer`. The handler gets the Player who sent it, then the arguments: `function(player, ...) ... end`. Scripts only.
---@field OnClientEvent Signal Fires when a Script calls `FireClient` or `FireAllClients`. The handler gets the arguments. LocalScripts only.
local RemoteEventClass = {}

---Sends the arguments to the server, where `OnServerEvent` fires with this player first. LocalScripts only.
---@param ... any
---@return nil
function RemoteEventClass:FireServer(...) end

---Sends the arguments to one player, where `OnClientEvent` fires. Scripts only.
---@param player Player
---@param ... any
---@return nil
function RemoteEventClass:FireClient(player, ...) end

---Sends the arguments to every player, where `OnClientEvent` fires. Scripts only.
---@param ... any
---@return nil
function RemoteEventClass:FireAllClients(...) end


---Someone playing the game, in Players. Made when they join.
---@class Player: Instance

---Groups the parts of one thing, such as a car or a house.
---@class Model: Instance

---Groups Instances to keep the tree tidy. Has no effect on the game.
---@class Folder: Instance

---Inside a MeshPart: the texture maps of one of its model's materials (MaterialName), drawn in place of the file's own. Delete it to go back to the file's.
---@class SurfaceAppearance: Instance
---@field MaterialName string The name of the material of the parent MeshPart's model whose maps this replaces. Import Model sets it.
---@field Color Color3 Multiplies the material's color (and its ColorMap).
---@field ColorMap string The base color texture, a file inside the project folder such as "assets/textures/wood.png". Empty for none.
---@field NormalMap string The normal map's file, for bumps and grooves. Empty for none.
---@field MetalnessMap string The metalness map's file (read from MetalnessChannel). Empty for the model's own metalness.
---@field RoughnessMap string The roughness map's file (read from RoughnessChannel). Empty for the model's own roughness.
---@field EmissiveMap string The file of colors the surface glows in. Empty for the model's own glow.
---@field AmbientOcclusionMap string The ambient occlusion map's file: dark where ambient light can't reach. Empty for none.
---@field OpacityMap string The opacity map's file (read from OpacityChannel): the surface is cut out where it's below half. Empty for the color map's alpha.
---@field SpecularMap string How strongly non-metal parts shine, for older materials: mid grey is the usual. Empty for none.
---@field NormalStrength number How far the normal map tips the surface: 1 as made, 0 flat.
---@field NormalMapDirectX boolean True for normal maps made for DirectX, whose green points the other way.
---@field MetalnessChannel EnumItem.TextureChannel|"Red"|"Green"|"Blue"|"Alpha" Which channel of MetalnessMap holds metalness, for packed textures.
---@field RoughnessChannel EnumItem.TextureChannel|"Red"|"Green"|"Blue"|"Alpha" Which channel of RoughnessMap holds roughness, for packed textures.
---@field InvertRoughness boolean True if RoughnessMap is a glossiness or smoothness map: white is smooth.
---@field AmbientOcclusionChannel EnumItem.TextureChannel|"Red"|"Green"|"Blue"|"Alpha" Which channel of AmbientOcclusionMap holds it, for packed textures.
---@field AmbientOcclusionStrength number How much AmbientOcclusionMap darkens, from 0 to 1.
---@field OpacityChannel EnumItem.TextureChannel|"Red"|"Green"|"Blue"|"Alpha" Which channel of OpacityMap holds opacity.
---@field InvertOpacity boolean True if OpacityMap is white where the surface is see-through.
---@field EmissiveStrength number Multiplies the glow.

---The on-screen UI root, usually inside Workspace.
---@class ScreenGui: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Enabled boolean If true, the UI in this ScreenGui is drawn.

---A rectangular UI element that can contain other UI elements.
---@class Frame: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The frame's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this frame and its children are hidden.

---A UI element that displays text.
---@class TextLabel: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The label's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Text string The text to display.
---@field TextColor3 Color3 The text color.
---@field TextSize number The text size in pixels.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this label is hidden.

---A UI element that displays text and fires Activated when clicked.
---@class TextButton: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The button's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Text string The text to display.
---@field TextColor3 Color3 The text color.
---@field TextSize number The text size in pixels.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this button is hidden and cannot be activated.
---@field Activated Signal Fires when the player clicks or taps this button. The handler gets no arguments; LocalScripts only.

---A UI element that displays an image from the project.
---@class ImageLabel: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The image label's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Image string The project-relative path of the image to display.
---@field ImageTransparency number The image opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this image is hidden.

---A sound effect or music track that scripts can play.
---@class Sound: Instance
---@field SoundId string The audio file inside the project folder, such as "assets/audio/chime.wav".
---@field Volume number Playback volume as a non-negative amplitude; 1 is the original level and 0 is silent.
---@field Looped boolean If true, playback repeats until Stop is called or the game session stops.
---@field PlaybackSpeed number How fast the sound plays: 1 is normal, 2 twice as fast (and an octave higher), 0.5 half. Changes apply while it plays.
---@field Playing boolean True while the sound plays. Set it to false to pause and true to carry on. Saved as true, the sound plays as soon as the game starts, with no script needed.
---@field Ended Signal Fires when the sound plays to its end. Looped sounds, and sounds stopped with Stop, don't fire it.
local SoundClass = {}

---Plays this sound from the start, with its SoundId, Volume, PlaybackSpeed and Looped, and sets Playing to true. Playing it again restarts it; stopping the game session stops all sounds.
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Play() end

---Stops this sound and sets Playing to false. The next Play starts from the beginning.
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Stop() end

---Pauses this sound where it is (sets Playing to false). Resume carries on from there.
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Pause() end

---Carries on playing a paused sound, or plays a stopped one from the start (sets Playing to true).
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Resume() end


---A light that shines in all directions from the center of its parent part.
---@class PointLight: Instance
---@field Enabled boolean If false, the light is off.
---@field Color Color3 The light's color.
---@field Brightness number How bright the light is.
---@field Range number How far the light reaches, in studs.

---A light that shines in a cone from the center of its parent part.
---@class SpotLight: Instance
---@field Enabled boolean If false, the light is off.
---@field Color Color3 The light's color.
---@field Brightness number How bright the light is.
---@field Range number How far the light reaches, in studs.
---@field Angle number The full width of the cone, in degrees.
---@field Direction Vector3 The way the beam points, relative to the parent part.

-- Globals -------------------------------------------------------------------

---The root of the game. Every service is inside it.
---@type DataModel
game = nil

---The service that holds the 3D world (same as `game.Workspace`).
---@type Workspace
workspace = nil

---The Script, LocalScript or ModuleScript that is running this code.
---@type Script|LocalScript|ModuleScript
script = nil

---Every enum, such as `Enum.Material`, `Enum.PartType` and `Enum.KeyCode`.
---@type EnumLibrary
Enum = nil

---Runs a ModuleScript (a `.module.lua` file, such as `require(game.ReplicatedStorage.Utils)`) the first time, and returns what it returned. Later calls on the same side return the same value.
---@param module Instance
---@return any
function require(module) end

---Creates Instances.
---@class InstanceLibrary
Instance = {}

---Creates an Instance of this class with default properties and no parent. Set `Parent` to put it in the world.
---@param className string
---@return Instance
---@overload fun(className: "Part"): Part
---@overload fun(className: "MeshPart"): MeshPart
---@overload fun(className: "Script"): Script
---@overload fun(className: "LocalScript"): LocalScript
---@overload fun(className: "ModuleScript"): ModuleScript
---@overload fun(className: "RemoteEvent"): RemoteEvent
